      "background_kind": "curated",
      "heading": "1 · Confidence is practiced",
      "sentence": "Creative confidence grows from doing creative work — not from waiting to feel gifted.",
      "quote": "Gifted, you may feel. Rehearse the method, you must.",
      "quote_origin": "tao_invented",
      "citation": {
        "label": "(Tao of Creativity)",
        "href": "/creativity-techniques-uem/lessons/en/creativity-techniques/u-6-personal-development/#tao-of-creativity"
      },
      "image_brief": "Confidence is practiced: returning to the canvas is the training.",
      "notes": "- Confidence follows action more often than the reverse.\n- U1's teachable creativity claim lands here as habit.\n- Do not confuse performance anxiety with lack of ability.\nSource: course wording; Beghetto/Karwowski/Kelley lines still pending page-level citation resolve.\nAsk: What did you finish this week that you can point to?",
      "claims": [],
      "asset_id": "wikimedia:File:Vincent van Gogh - Self-Portrait - Google Art Project (454045).jpg",
      "media_slot_id": "U6.masterclass-1"
    },
    {
      "slide_id": "masterclass-2",
      "slide_role": "masterclass",
      "background_kind": "curated",
      "heading": "2 · Beliefs convert potential",
      "sentence": "Believing you can and should act creatively turns ability into action under a real brief.",
      "image_brief": "Beliefs convert potential: the etcher sits down to work as if the work matters.",
      "notes": "- Creative confidence and centrality beliefs both matter.\n- Potential without action stays potential.\n- Briefs give a lawful place to act.\nSource: course wording.\nAsk: Which belief stopped you last month — can, or should?",
      "claims": [],
      "asset_id": "wikimedia:File:Self-Portrait etching at a window (SM 61530d).png",
      "media_slot_id": "U6.masterclass-2"
    },
    {
