      "slide_role": "masterclass",
      "background_kind": "curated",
      "heading": "3 · Mastery feeds regulation",
      "sentence": "Success experiences teach what to repeat, revise, or drop — they train self-regulation.",
      "image_brief": "Mastery feeds regulation: quiet skilled repetition teaches what to keep.",
      "notes": "- Mastery here means useful feedback from your own work, not perfection.\n- Regulation is choosing the next move on purpose.\n- Pair with reflection logs, not mood tracking.\nSource: course wording.\nAsk: What small success will you repeat on purpose next week?",
      "claims": [],
      "asset_id": "wikimedia:File:Johannes Vermeer - A Lady Writing - Google Art Project.jpg",
